# Intent: the mint face's two privacy looks (owner: a muted mouth looks different, no-vision eyes look different, never an X because it looks dead). MintMouth::setSealed(true) draws one flat closed line whatever the emotion or the lip sync says; MintEye::setLowered(true) replaces the round dot with a calm half-lidded eye (the lower half of the disc, a little low so it looks down). Both persist across emotions, so the muted mouth stays through blinks, replies and the idle expression; the happy, angry and sleepy eye shapes keep their own drawing. The palette recolor reaches the new arc, and MintAvatar::inkColor() lets the display draw its full-quiet marker in the live ink color.
# Upstream: firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/mint/mint.{h,cpp} (MIT). Applies after 013. The display calls these from patch 105.
# Check after a flash: mute: the mouth is a flat line while the eyes blink and the idle look-around goes on; vision off: both eyes are half discs; change the face color in Home and both keep up with the palette; speak a reply while muted from the host and the mouth stays flat.
